  ],
  "text": "Coral cannot catch enough food to survive. So it farms instead. It is an animal, by the way. Not a rock, and not a plant. Each polyp is a tiny animal with a mouth and tentacles, sitting in a stone cup. Inside its body it keeps algae. They photosynthesise and hand the sugar over. That arrangement is where nearly all of the coral's food comes from. Warm the water by two degrees and the arrangement breaks. The polyp throws the algae out. It is a stress response, not a choice. So bleaching is not paint fading. That white is the skeleton showing through. Reefs cover under one percent of the seafloor and house a quarter of everything in the sea. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
